134-        <h3 class="text-2xl text-gray-700 font-semibold mb-4">Empowerment &amp; CPIO Designation</h3>
135-        <p class="text-gray-800 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
136:            For operational clarity and effective functioning, the Central Admission Committee (CAC) is empowered by the University Admission Coordination Board (UACB) to oversee the printing and publication of all official prospectuses, application forms, bulletins, and advertisements related to University admissions. All decisions made by the CAC will be reported to the UACB promptly for record.
137-        </p>
138-        <p class="text-gray-800 text-lg leading-relaxed">
139:            Furthermore, the Member Secretary of the Central Admission Committee is officially designated as the **Central Public Information Officer (CPIO)** under the provisions of the Right to Information (RTI) Act 2005 for all activities of the CAC. This designation is in addition to the duties of the Member Secretary within the Academic Section. The Deputy Registrar (Academic) is appointed to serve as the **First Appellate Authority** in this regard.
140-        </p>
